{"tool_name":"focus","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"focus","identifiers":[],"license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"FOCUS is an innovative and agile model to profile and report organisms present in metagenomic samples based on composition usage without sequence length dependencies.","home_url":"https://edwards.sdsu.edu/FOCUS","keywords":["Metagenome"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":5},"biotools":{"id":"focus","home":"https://github.com/metageni/FOCUS","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"FOCUS (Find Organisms by Composition Usage) is an agile profiler for metagenomic data.","addition_date":"2021-06-04T12:38:35Z","last_update_date":"2021-06-04T13:03:34Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:focus","credit":[{"email":"genivaldo.gueiros@gmail.com","name":"Genivaldo Gueiros Z. Silva","url":"https://edwards.sdsu.edu/geni/"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/metageni/FOCUS#usage"},{"type":["Installation instructions"],"url":"https://github.com/metageni/FOCUS#installation"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2044"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"},{"term":"FASTQ","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1930"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Deposition","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3431"}]},{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2044"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"},{"term":"FASTQ","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1930"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"k-mer counting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3472"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Taxonomic classification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1872"},"format":[{"term":"TSV","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3475"}]}]}],"name":"FOCUS","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Kigaard","publication":[{"doi":"10.7717/peerj.425","metadata":{"abstract":"One of the major goals in metagenomics is to identify the organisms present in a microbial community fromunannotated shotgun sequencing reads. Taxonomic profiling has valuable applications in biological and medical research, including disease diagnostics. Most currently available approaches do not scale well with increasing data volumes, which is important because both the number and lengths of the reads provided by sequencing platforms keep increasing. Here we introduce FOCUS, an agile composition based approach using non-negative least squares (NNLS) to report the organisms present in metagenomic samples and profile their abundances. FOCUS was tested with simulated and real metagenomes, and the results show that our approach accurately predicts the organisms present in microbial communities. FOCUS was implemented in Python. The source code and web-sever are freely available at http://edwards.sdsu.edu/FOCUS. \u00a9 2014 Silva et al.","authors":[{"name":"Cuevas D.A."},{"name":"Dutilh B.E."},{"name":"Edwards R.A."},{"name":"Silva G.G.Z."}],"citationCount":45,"date":"2014-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"PeerJ","title":"FOCUS: An alignment-free model to identify organisms in metagenomes using non-negative least squares"},"pmcid":"PMC4060023","pmid":"24949242","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Metagenomic sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3837"},{"term":"Metagenomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3174"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"FOCUS","home":"https://bio.tools/focus","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"FOCUS (Find Organisms by Composition Usage) is an agile profiler for metagenomic data.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:focus/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registratio